<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Nationalist government</h1><p class="st-meta">1925 CE – 1948 CE · capital Guangzhou, Nanjing, Chongqing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Kuomintang government of the Republic of China, which reunified the country in 1928 and led its resistance to Japan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen's</a> death the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-military-government">Canton Military Government</a> was reorganised in July 1925 as the National Government under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>. Its armies, trained at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/whampoa-military-academy">Whampoa</a>, set out on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a> in 1926, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> broke with the Communists in 1927, he established the government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in 1928.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In theory a period of one-party tutelage before constitutional rule, the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> decade' brought new roads, railways, a national currency and modern schools, but regional warlords kept power and the government fought a long war against the Communists. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> in 1931. After full-scale war began in 1937 the government moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chongqing">Chongqing</a>, which survived years of bombing; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> became one of the Allied powers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> surrender, civil war with the Communists resumed. A constitution took effect, and in May 1948 the National Government gave way to constitutional government with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang</a> as president. Defeated on the mainland, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a> moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> in 1949.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nationalist-government.jpg" alt="Nationalist government" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Sekisama · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Emblem_of_the_Republic_of_China.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1925 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guangzhou, Nanjing, Chongqing</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wang Jingwei, Chiang Kai-shek, Lin Sen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a>, <a href="/countries/taiwan">Taiwan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>National Government of the Republic of China, Nanjing government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1936&amp;focus=nationalist-government" aria-label="Nationalist government on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7705 1324 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nationalist government lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8025 1580L7868 1006M8025 1580L8025 1580M8025 1580L8221 1549"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7868 1006h0M8025 1580h0M8221 1549h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8025 1580h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8025 1580h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guangzhou. <a href="/atlas?year=1936&amp;focus=nationalist-government">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
